      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63834,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients present with abnormal uterine bleeding, pelvic pain/pressure, or a uterine mass.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-07T14:15:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63835,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>These tumours are rare {30324234}. Patients range in age from 14 to 71&nbsp;years, but patients with <em>BCOR</em> internal tandem duplication (ITD) high-grade endometrial stromal sarcomas are typically younger (median age: 44&nbsp;years; range: 14&ndash;59&nbsp;years), although only a few cases have been reported.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:21:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63836,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:04:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63837,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours harbour <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2A/B</em> fusions {22223660; 22456610; 23599159; 24592973; 27219024; 28390819}, <em>ZC3H7B</em>-<em>BCOR</em> fusions {23580382; 29192652; 27631520; 30789359}, or <em>BCOR</em>&nbsp;ITD&nbsp;{29200103; 28621321; 30380541}. <em>EPC1</em>-<em>BCOR</em>, <em>JAZF1</em>-<em>BCORL1</em>, and <em>BRD8</em>-<em>PHF1</em> fusions are rare {30144186; 28331900; 30789359}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:21:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63838,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>High-grade endometrial stromal sarcomas are typically bulky, intracavitary or intramural, tan-yellow, fleshy masses, often displaying haemorrhage and necrosis {22456610; 25355621; 29192652; 30380541}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:04:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63839,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours may show expansile, permeative, or infiltrative growth, and more than one pattern of invasion may be seen. They typically display lymphovascular invasion, brisk mitotic activity, and necrosis. Tumours with <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2A/B</em> fusion display round cells with eosinophilic cytoplasm and high-grade nuclei with irregular nuclear contours, vesicular chromatin, and variably distinct nucleoli. They may be associated with a fibromyxoid or conventional low-grade endometrial stromal component {22456610; 23599159; 25355621; 28863072}. Pseudopapillary/glandular architecture, rhabdoid morphology, pseudorosettes, and sex cord&ndash;like differentiation are rare {21737666; 22456610}. The high-grade component is positive for cyclin&nbsp;D1, BCOR, KIT, CD56, and CD99, and negative for DOG1 {24186140; 22456610; 28621321}.</p>\r\n<p><em>ZC3H7B</em>-<em>BCOR</em> high-grade sarcomas are typically positive for cyclin&nbsp;D1, whereas only about 50% of cases express BCOR. They typically show diffuse CD10 positivity with variable ER and PR positivity. They may also show focal expression of SMA and caldesmon but are negative for desmin. Tumours may show pan-TRK staining but it is unrelated to NTRK rearrangement {31375766}. <em>BCOR</em>&nbsp;ITD tumours have a different immunoprofile than <em>ZC3H7B</em>-<em>BCOR</em> tumours (only a few cases reported): they may be less positive for CD10, and they are typically diffusely positive for cyclin&nbsp;D1 and BCOR and negative for ER and PR. Furthermore, they may express desmin but are negative for SMA and caldesmon {29192652; 29200103; 28621321}. High-grade endometrial stromal sarcoma NOS is a high-grade sarcoma associated with a low-grade endometrial stromal component {18580489}. <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/246/10706\" target=\"_blank\">#10706</a>Table&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/246/10706\" target=\"_blank\">#10706</a> summarizes the immunophenotype for all of these tumours {29192652; 28621321; 27631520; 22456610; 22982899; 30252726}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:21:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63840,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:04:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63841,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "<p>Demonstration of gene fusion or ITD may be helpful for diagnosis. High-grade endometrial stromal sarcomas harbour <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2A/B</em> fusions {22223660; 22456610; 23599159; 24592973; 27219024; 28390819}, <em>ZC3H7B</em>-<em>BCOR</em> fusions {23580382; 29192652; 27631520; 30789359}, or <em>BCOR</em>&nbsp;ITD {29200103; 28621321; 30380541}. <em>EPC1</em>-<em>BCOR</em>, <em>JAZF1</em>-<em>BCORL1</em>, and <em>BRD8</em>-<em>PHF1</em> fusions are rare {30144186; 28331900; 30789359}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:22:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63842,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> monomorphic high-grade round and/or spindle cells; brisk mitotic activity; cyclin&nbsp;D1 and BCOR immunohistochemical positivity if <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2A/B</em> or <em>ZC3H7B</em>-<em>BCOR</em> fusion or <em>BCOR</em> ITD; a low-grade endometrial stromal component if NOS.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> confirmatory genotype in selected cases.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:22:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63843,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This entity is staged as uterine sarcoma using the FIGO, Union for International Cancer Control (UICC), and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:04:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63844,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>High-grade endometrial stromal sarcomas are more aggressive than low-grade endometrial stromal sarcomas. Anthracycline-based therapy may benefit patients with recurrent <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2A/B</em> sarcoma {28390819}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:04:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]